Composer-dock collapse verdict fixed (own code). The readout is meant to degrade to
its icon when the row cannot fit the full reading, but it never fired: the verdict
read `parent.clientWidth` — the WHOLE row — and compared the full reading against
it. The plugin is one entry in that row (the official usage pill and context ring
sit beside it), so on the live ~860px row with ~260px taken by the official pair,
600px of reading compared against 860px and always "fit". The two figures the docs
promised — the official siblings and the gaps — were never subtracted.

`client/dockRow.ts` now holds that arithmetic as a pure function (`roomForEntry`:
content box minus the siblings minus one gap per sibling, `null` when the row is
unmeasurable so a bogus environment keeps the full reading instead of collapsing),
and `composerDock.tsx` feeds it the row's padding, its non-trigger children and its
`column-gap`. The siblings must contribute the width they NEED, not the box they
currently occupy: the official pills are compressible (`min-width: 0` + ellipsis)
while this readout is `flex: none`, so a row that is too small squeezes them first.
Charging only their squashed box inverted the verdict — the more they were squeezed,
the more room this line believed it had, so it stayed full and kept squeezing them
(live: the officials read "4 ..." and "46...." while this line was untouched).
`naturalWidthOf` supplies the needed width (box plus whatever the element and its
clipping descendants are hiding), which does not move with flex allocation and so
cannot feed back. The measuring probe also gained the row's own box metrics — the 14px
glyph, the 6px gap and the `1px 8px` padding — because as a bare text span it
under-measured the reading by ~36px and left borderline rows one size too long.

For reference, the official component this row neighbours
(`ui-chat/src/client/chat/StatsPills.tsx`) does no measurement at all: it has no
`ResizeObserver`, `offsetWidth`, `getBoundingClientRect`, `clientWidth`,
`matchMedia` or `useEffect`, and shrinks purely in CSS (`.root`/`.pill`
`min-width:0;max-width:100%` plus `.label` ellipsis). Degrading to an icon is this
fork's own, stronger fallback, so the arithmetic it needs is this fork's to own.

The verdict also never RE-RAN at the right moment (own code). Fixing the arithmetic
was not enough, because the plugin's own data (the timeline) arrives first: its
effect runs while its row holds only itself, computes "room 495px vs need 237px —
fits", and the official pills and context ring then mount on their own schedule.
That does not resize the row (a flex row's width comes from its parent; measured in
Chrome: 495px before and after), so the `ResizeObserver` on the row never fired
(callback count 0) and the verdict stayed frozen at "fits" for the life of the
mount. Only a window resize re-ran it. The observer set therefore gained a
`MutationObserver` on the row with `childList: true` — the one scope that catches
sibling entries mounting while ignoring this button's own form toggle, which would
otherwise feed back. Verified in Chrome with the officials mounting asynchronously
on a 495px row: the verdict re-runs on the child-list change, the readout collapses,
and the official pills stop being ellipsised.
